# Extra specs for the `rocm-gfx90a` flavor (one per line; `#` comments allowed).
# Added via `spack add` on top of the base environment. amdgpu_target=gfx90a
# comes from flavors/rocm-gfx90a.yaml (applied only to packages that expose it).
#
# NOTE: unlike CUDA (spack's `cuda` is a fast binary installer), `hip` builds the
# whole ROCm stack FROM SOURCE — llvm-amdgpu (AMD's clang fork), hsa-rocr-dev,
# comgr, hipcc, rocm-core, ... The first build is heavy (hours, disk-hungry);
# afterwards it is pulled from the OCI buildcache like everything else.

# ROCm HIP toolchain. This single package transitively pulls llvm-amdgpu +
# runtime + tools; there is no separate `rocm` umbrella package.
hip

# traccc GPU stack, verified variant names:
#   vecmem  -> its own `+hip` variant     (depends_on hip when +hip)
#   covfie  -> spack ROCmPackage `+rocm`  (NOT +hip; maps to COVFIE_PLATFORM_HIP)
vecmem +hip
covfie +rocm

# TODO(gpu): validate against the pinned Spack before re-adding. algebra-plugins
# errored as "no such package" on the CUDA run; detray/traccc HIP backends and
# their exact variant names are unconfirmed. Likely need custom package.py under
# spack_repo/acts/packages/.
#   algebra-plugins +vc
#   detray +rocm
